{"agency_id": "whaikaha", "canonical_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HVZNg1a2cuY", "captured_at": "2026-07-07T10:17:40+00:00", "content": "Acknowledging the passing of Stephanie Āwheto\n\nWhaikaha, and the New Zealand Sign Language Board, wish to acknowledge the passing of Stephanie Āwheto over the weekend.\n\nStephanie (Ngāti Ruanui/Taranaki descent) was the first trilingual (te reo Māori, NZSL and English) interpreter in Aotearoa and helped to create and modify signs to reflect Te Ao Māori.\n\nWe mourn Stephanie’s passing and celebrate her life, influence, and contribution as an advocate, educator, and interpreter.\n\nOur thoughts go out to Stephanie’s whānau, friends and the Tūri (Deaf) Māori community.", "content_hash": "314a783abd29155627c551512d189e35a1f16840a0bff1c88eb4d30bf2e1ca13", "cross_source_ids": {"channel_id": "UCcpShDCWICteXnheXsk6Qog", "feed_url": "https://www.youtube.com/feeds/videos.xml?channel_id=UCcpShDCWICteXnheXsk6Qog", "source_id": "17f168a37d2bfae3", "video_id": "HVZNg1a2cuY"}, "extraction_method": "generic_registered_youtube_channel_rss", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2024-07-08T01:52:09+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw\\youtube\\2024-07\\ba9ea21d7eb8682192cf56d2.json", "record_id": "youtube:ba9ea21d7eb8682192cf56d2", "source_account": "WhaikahaNZ", "source_kind": "social_profile", "source_platform": "youtube", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@WhaikahaNZ"}
{"agency_id": "whaikaha", "canonical_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HVZNg1a2cuY", "captured_at": "2026-07-07T10:17:40+00:00", "content": "Acknowledging the passing of Stephanie Āwheto\n\nWhaikaha, and the New Zealand Sign Language Board, wish to acknowledge the passing of Stephanie Āwheto over the weekend.\n\nStephanie (Ngāti Ruanui/Taranaki descent) was the first trilingual (te reo Māori, NZSL and English) interpreter in Aotearoa and helped to create and modify signs to reflect Te Ao Māori.\n\nWe mourn Stephanie’s passing and celebrate her life, influence, and contribution as an advocate, educator, and interpreter.\n\nOur thoughts go out to Stephanie’s whānau, friends and the Tūri (Deaf) Māori community.", "content_hash": "314a783abd29155627c551512d189e35a1f16840a0bff1c88eb4d30bf2e1ca13", "cross_source_ids": {"channel_id": "UCcpShDCWICteXnheXsk6Qog", "feed_url": "https://www.youtube.com/feeds/videos.xml?channel_id=UCcpShDCWICteXnheXsk6Qog", "source_id": "whaikaha-youtube-dd017439", "video_id": "HVZNg1a2cuY"}, "extraction_method": "generic_registered_youtube_channel_rss", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2024-07-08T01:52:09+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw\\youtube\\2024-07\\d09f5969c4253ed59fac18c3.json", "record_id": "youtube:d09f5969c4253ed59fac18c3", "source_account": "YouTube page", "source_kind": "social_profile", "source_platform": "youtube", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCcpShDCWICteXnheXsk6Qog"}
